Z||000000||jerpro||02-07-2001||10:16 AM||||I test drove my 87 yesterday and did an overall check with a snapon machine. Everything seems fine except the fan.<BR>MY coolant level was up to 198 and the fan did not kick in. I didn't have any overheating problems at all when I dorve it (alas air-dam) but am concerned that I might have to replace the fan motor. <BR>Any experience or know what should I do?<BR>I thought of unpluggin the wires and de-carbonize them to see if it's jst a bad concection, but I will have to do that next week as my car is  stored 1hr 1/2 from where I live<BR>thanks<BR>||||reg||9
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||02-07-2001||10:22 AM||||In stock setups the fan switch will not normally kick in till temp. reaches 230 degrees F.||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroJoe||02-07-2001||10:32 AM||||Do you have AC?  If you do, turn it on with the car parked and running.  The fan will come on if the AC is on and the car's speed is below 35mph.<P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR>AIM: Fiero87311, Snowboarder0311<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||87GT||02-07-2001||12:45 PM||||If the car starts to run hot, the fan wont kick on until about 220 to 230.  ||||reg||1
